# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=gift spec=warlock:destruction style=auto
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=844x390,touch save=carried (behaves as
# fresh, #273 -- carried never actually carries across separate playbot
# invocations because the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
# `boss=gift` is a coverage label only (direction.md's 2026-09-25 note on
# playpick.ts): a mode=walk evening steers at no named boss, the walk starts
# at the door same as any other.
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: the one prior style=auto evening
# (2026-09-26-40, druid:feral, same size/difficulty/viewport) was a melee dps
# that never approaches anything. warlock:destruction is a pure ranged caster
# -- its whole kit casts from range, so a body that never steers (auto's own
# already-confirmed lack of a movement term) may still be able to fight
# without ever closing distance, unlike the melee case. This is the first
# time this line can separate "auto never moves" from "auto never damages"
# by role.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:warlock:destruction
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening auto 200 5
state
shot mid
says
bill
